{"id":"G3705","lemma":"ὅραμα","transliteration":"horama","sayIt":"horama","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, neuter","gloss":"vision","meaning":"ὅραμα, -τος, τό\n(ὁράω), [in LXX for חָזוֹן, מַרְאֶה, etc. ;]\nthat which is seen;\n(a) a sight, spectacle: Mat.17:9, Act.7:31;\n(b) an appearance, vision: Act.9:10, 12 (Rec.) Act.10:3, 17 10:19 11:5 12:9 16:9-10 18:9 (cf. ὀπτασία).†\n(AS)","glosses":["vision","sight","had a clear vision"],"count":12,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-17","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"vision","kjv":"the vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-7","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"sight","kjv":"at the sight"}},{"chapterId":"act-9","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision","kjv":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-9","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision","kjv":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-10","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"he had a clear vision","kjv":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-10","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"vision","kjv":"this vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-10","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"vision","kjv":"the vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-11","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision","kjv":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-12","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-16","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision","kjv":"a vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-16","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"vision","kjv":"the vision"}},{"chapterId":"act-18","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"a vision","kjv":"a vision"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 17:9","note":"As they were coming down from the mountain, Jesus commanded them, saying, “Don’t tell anyone what you saw, until the Son of Man has risen from the dead.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 7:31","note":"When Moses saw it, he wondered at the sight. As he came close to see, a voice of the Lord came to him,","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G3701","lemma":"ὀπτασία","transliteration":"optasia","gloss":"vision"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}